{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Orgo API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "summary": "Provision and control cloud computers (virtual desktops) for AI agents.",
    "description": "REST API for Orgo: cloud computers for AI agents. Authenticate with a Bearer API key. Full reference and SDK guides: https://docs.orgo.ai.",
    "termsOfService": "https://www.orgo.ai/terms",
    "contact": {
      "name": "Orgo",
      "url": "https://www.orgo.ai"
    }
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://www.orgo.ai",
      "description": "Production"
    }
  ],
  "externalDocs": {
    "description": "Orgo developer docs",
    "url": "https://docs.orgo.ai"
  },
  "security": [
    {
      "bearerApiKey": []
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/api/health": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "getHealth",
        "summary": "Liveness probe",
        "security": [],
        "tags": [
          "system"
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Service is healthy."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/me": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "getMe",
        "summary": "Current authenticated account",
        "tags": [
          "account"
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Account profile and tier."
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/account/capacity": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "getAccountCapacity",
        "summary": "What the account may run, runs and has added, and how many of each size it may still add",
        "tags": [
          "account"
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "computers, ram_gb and vcpu ({ limit, in_use }; vcpu is the account vCPU pool, with no limit when unmetered), added, self_serve_cap, can_add per size (0 for 2xl unless past_xl_allowed), past_xl_allowed (whether computers past XL, more than 6 vCPU or 32 GB, are the account’s to add and create; false: set up on request), sizes with monthly prices and the vCPU each launches with, rates per term (ram_gb_usd, vcpu_usd, disk_20gb_usd, computer_usd, windows_usd: the per-part prices any shape is billed at) and per_computer_max."
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "A workspace-scoped key: capacity needs an account-wide key."
          }
        }
      },
      "post": {
        "operationId": "addAccountCapacity",
        "summary": "Add computers on the card on file, or price them first (dry_run)",
        "description": "Body: a size ({ \"size\": \"small\" | \"medium\" | \"large\" | \"xl\" | \"2xl\" }), any shape ({ \"ram_gb\", \"vcpu\", \"disk_gb\" }, all three), or a size with parts replaced ({ \"size\": \"medium\", \"vcpu\": 1 } is 8 GB, 1 vCPU, 40 GB); plus \"count\": 1-500, \"os\"?: \"linux\" | \"windows\", \"term\"?: \"monthly\" | \"yearly\", \"dry_run\"?: boolean. ram_gb is 4, 8, 16, 32 or 64, vcpu 0.5, 1, 2, 4, 6 or 8, disk_gb 20 to 300 in steps of 20: the shapes a computer can be created with. Every shape is billed at the same per-part rates (GET rates). Past XL (2xl, ram_gb 64, or vcpu 8) is set up on request on every plan: 403 CONTACT_US_FOR_SIZE with max_cpu and max_ram_gb, dry runs included, unless the account is on Enterprise or its negotiated plan goes past XL (GET past_xl_allowed). Send an Idempotency-Key header (a UUID) so a retry answers again instead of buying twice. Bounded by the account’s self-serve cap; past it the answer is 403 capacity_cap and the cap can be raised for the account.\n\nOr add memory, vCPU or storage on their own to the account’s pool, with no computer: { \"addon\": { \"vcpu\": 4, \"ram_gb\": 16, \"disk_gb\": 100 } }, amounts to add (vCPU in 0.5 steps, RAM in whole GB, disk in 20 GB steps), with term and dry_run as above and nothing else. Every computer draws from the pool.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "oneOf": [
                  {
                    "title": "Computers",
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "count"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "size": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "enum": [
                          "small",
                          "medium",
                          "large",
                          "xl",
                          "2xl"
                        ]
                      },
                      "ram_gb": {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "enum": [
                          4,
                          8,
                          16,
                          32,
                          64
                        ]
                      },
                      "vcpu": {
                        "type": "number",
                        "enum": [
                          0.5,
                          1,
                          2,
                          4,
                          6,
                          8
                        ]
                      },
                      "disk_gb": {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "minimum": 20,
                        "maximum": 300,
                        "multipleOf": 20
                      },
                      "count": {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "minimum": 1,
                        "maximum": 500
                      },
                      "os": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "enum": [
                          "linux",
                          "windows"
                        ]
                      },
                      "term": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "enum": [
                          "monthly",
                          "yearly"
                        ]
                      },
                      "dry_run": {
                        "type": "boolean"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Memory, vCPU or storage",
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "addon"
                    ],
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "properties": {
                      "addon": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "additionalProperties": false,
                        "minProperties": 1,
                        "properties": {
                          "vcpu": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
                            "maximum": 1000,
                            "multipleOf": 0.5
                          },
                          "ram_gb": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "minimum": 1,
                            "maximum": 8000
                          },
                          "disk_gb": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "minimum": 20,
                            "maximum": 100000,
                            "multipleOf": 20
                          }
                        }
                      },
                      "term": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "enum": [
                          "monthly",
                          "yearly"
                        ]
                      },
                      "dry_run": {
                        "type": "boolean"
                      }
                    },
                    "example": {
                      "addon": {
                        "vcpu": 4
                      },
                      "dry_run": true
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "tags": [
          "account"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "Idempotency-Key",
            "in": "header",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 8,
              "maxLength": 255
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Added (or, for dry_run, priced), with the account’s capacity after it."
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Invalid request."
          },
          "402": {
            "description": "No paid plan (no_subscription), or the card was declined (card_declined)."
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "Past the self-serve cap (capacity_cap), past XL (CONTACT_US_FOR_SIZE, with max_cpu and max_ram_gb), or a workspace-scoped key."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "A request with this Idempotency-Key is running, or did not finish."
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "This Idempotency-Key was used for a different request."
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "Rate limited."
          }
        }
      },
      "patch": {
        "operationId": "reduceAccountCapacity",
        "summary": "Keep this many added computers from the next renewal",
        "description": "Body: { \"added_computers\": n }. The current period is paid for, so the reduction takes effect at renewal.",
        "tags": [
          "account"
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The scheduled reduction and the account’s capacity."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Running computers use that capacity (in_use)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/agents": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "agentSignup",
        "summary": "Anonymous agent signup: a new account and its API key in one call",
        "description": "No authentication. Body (optional): { \"name\"?: string (1-80), \"contact_email\"?: string }. Makes an unclaimed account with a workspace and an account-wide API key, shown once. Unclaimed accounts start with no credit and run one Medium Linux computer by the hour from credits they add (see POST /api/v1/credits), hold at most 3 keys, and cannot invite people, publish public URLs, add domains, create client accounts or invoice. They expire 72 hours after signup unless a person opens claim.url and claims them. Send an Idempotency-Key header (a UUID) so a retry answers the same account. Answers 404 where agent signup is off.",
        "tags": [
          "auth"
        ],
        "security": [],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "Idempotency-Key",
            "in": "header",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 8,
              "maxLength": 255
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": false,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "name": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "maxLength": 80
                  },
                  "contact_email": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "format": "email",
                    "maxLength": 320
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "{ api_key, key_id, account: { id, name, workspace_id, workspace_name, status: \"unclaimed\", expires_at }, claim: { url, code, expires_at }, limits, next, message }."
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Invalid body or Idempotency-Key."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Agent signup is off here (agent_signup_disabled)."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "A request with this Idempotency-Key is running, or did not finish."
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "This Idempotency-Key was used for a different request."
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "Rate limited per address, per network, or the daily cap (rate_limited, Retry-After)."
          },
          "503": {
            "description": "Unavailable; retry after Retry-After."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/agents/claim": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "getAgentClaimStatus",
        "summary": "This agent account’s status (unclaimed, claimed, expired) and expiry",
        "tags": [
          "auth"
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "{ account: { id, workspace_id, status, expires_at, claimed_at } }."
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "The key is not an agent account’s (not_agent_account)."
          }
        }
      },
      "post": {
        "operationId": "refreshAgentClaimLink",
        "summary": "A new claim link for this agent account; the previous link stops working",
        "tags": [
          "auth"
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "{ claim: { url, code, expires_at }, account }."
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "A workspace-scoped key: use the account-wide key from signup."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "The key is not an agent account’s."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Already claimed."
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "Rate limited."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/keys": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "listApiKeys",
        "summary": "List this account’s API keys (no plaintext)",
        "tags": [
          "auth"
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "API key metadata."
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          }
        }
      },
      "post": {
        "operationId": "createApiKey",
        "summary": "Create an API key (optionally workspace-scoped)",
        "tags": [
          "auth"
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Newly created key (plaintext shown once)."
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/workspaces": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "listWorkspaces",
        "summary": "List workspaces (projects) for the account",
        "tags": [
          "workspaces"
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Array of workspaces."
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          }
        }
      },
      "post": {
        "operationId": "createWorkspace",
        "summary": "Create a workspace",
        "tags": [
          "workspaces"
        ],
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Created workspace."
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "listComputers",
        "summary": "List cloud computers (virtual desktops)",
        "tags": [
          "computers"
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Array of computers."
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          }
        }
      },
      "post": {
        "operationId": "createComputer",
        "summary": "Provision a new cloud computer (optionally from a template via template_ref)",
        "description": "With no size the computer is 4 GB RAM and 1 vCPU. A ram with no cpu gets that size’s vCPU (8 GB: 2, 16 GB: 4, 32 GB: 6, 64 GB: 8). An explicit cpu is used as given; cpu 16 passes the value check and is refused with 403 PER_COMPUTER_CPU_CAP (8 is the most one computer runs). With template_ref and no cpu/ram the template’s own size applies, with at least the vCPU of its RAM’s size (an 8 GB template launches with 2). vCPU is an account pool shared by the owner’s computers. A computer past XL (more than 6 vCPU or 32 GB, so 2XL: 8 vCPU, 64 GB), asked for or brought by a template, is set up on request on every plan: 403 CONTACT_US_FOR_SIZE with max_cpu and max_ram_gb, unless the workspace owner is on Enterprise or has a negotiated plan that goes past XL (GET /api/billing/compute-limits past_xl_allowed). Clones and hourly launches of 2XL follow the same rule.",
        "tags": [
          "computers"
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CreateComputer"
              },
              "example": {
                "workspace_id": "6f1c2a7e-3b9d-4c1a-9e2f-0a1b2c3d4e5f",
                "name": "agent-1",
                "os": "linux",
                "ram": 8
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Created computer."
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "A value outside the allowed sets (os, ram, cpu, gpu), or disk_size_gb above what the computer may have (disk_exceeds_quota)."
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          },
          "402": {
            "description": "An hourly launch the account’s credit cannot fund."
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "The owner’s plan cannot fund this computer: UPGRADE_REQUIRED (no paid plan), VM_SLOT_ADDON (computer count), RAM_ADDON (RAM), VCPU_ADDON (the account vCPU pool), PER_COMPUTER_RAM_CAP or PER_COMPUTER_CPU_CAP (above what one computer runs), CONTACT_US_FOR_SIZE (past XL, set up on request; with max_cpu and max_ram_gb), PLAN_LIMIT (a plan negotiated with Orgo), WINDOWS_REQUIRES_SCALE, or CLIENT_PRICE_EXCEEDED (a workspace its client pays for). Carries canManageCapacity, and upgradeTier where a plan change would fix it.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "template_ref given but the template golden is not built, or the name is taken (NAME_TAKEN)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/public-urls": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "listPublicUrls",
        "summary": "List a computer’s public URLs",
        "description": "A public URL is https://<label>.<base_domain> (orgo.dev) serving a port inside the computer to anyone with the link. The app must listen on 0.0.0.0:<port>, not 127.0.0.1. Answers { enabled: false, public_urls: [] } where the feature is off or the computer cannot have one (only Linux and Windows computers can).",
        "tags": [
          "public-urls"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Settings and the list.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PublicUrlList"
                },
                "example": {
                  "enabled": true,
                  "base_domain": "orgo.dev",
                  "limit": 5,
                  "public_urls": [
                    {
                      "id": "6f1c2a7e-3b9d-4c1a-9e2f-0a1b2c3d4e5f",
                      "url": "https://cool-thing.orgo.dev",
                      "hostname": "cool-thing.orgo.dev",
                      "label": "cool-thing",
                      "port": 3000,
                      "created_at": "2026-10-05T18:00:00.000Z"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "No access to this computer, or a share-link guest."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Computer not found."
          }
        }
      },
      "post": {
        "operationId": "createPublicUrl",
        "summary": "Make a public URL for a port on the computer",
        "description": "Body: { \"port\": 1-65535, \"label\"?: string }. The label is lowercased; 3-40 letters, digits and hyphens, starting and ending with a letter or digit, not all digits, no hyphens in the third and fourth places (ab--), not a reserved name, not shaped like a computer id (8 hex characters or orgo-...). Without one, a name like brave-otter-3f2a is picked. Ports 22, 3389, 5900, 6080, 8080 and 9000 belong to the computer and are refused. Errors are { error, code }. The app must listen on 0.0.0.0:<port>. Cookies the app sets are host-only (a Domain attribute other than the URL’s own hostname is removed).",
        "tags": [
          "public-urls"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CreatePublicUrl"
              },
              "example": {
                "port": 3000,
                "label": "cool-thing"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Created.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PublicUrl"
                },
                "example": {
                  "id": "6f1c2a7e-3b9d-4c1a-9e2f-0a1b2c3d4e5f",
                  "url": "https://cool-thing.orgo.dev",
                  "hostname": "cool-thing.orgo.dev",
                  "label": "cool-thing",
                  "port": 3000,
                  "created_at": "2026-10-05T18:00:00.000Z"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Bad port (INVALID_PORT), bad label (INVALID_LABEL), or a computer that cannot have one (PUBLIC_URLS_UNSUPPORTED).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "Port 8080 is used by the computer itself and cannot be shared. Run your app on another port.",
                  "code": "INVALID_PORT"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "No access to this computer, or a share-link guest."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Public URLs are not enabled here, or the computer was not found.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "public URLs are not enabled"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "The name is taken (LABEL_TAKEN), the computer has as many public URLs as it may (PUBLIC_URL_LIMIT), or the account does, across all its computers (PUBLIC_URL_ACCOUNT_LIMIT, 10 by default).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "This computer already has 5 public URLs, the most it can have. Remove one to add another.",
                  "code": "PUBLIC_URL_LIMIT"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "Too many public URLs made today by this user (RATE_LIMITED). Retry-After says when to try again.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "503": {
            "description": "No free generated name was found. Try again."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/public-urls/{urlId}": {
      "patch": {
        "operationId": "updatePublicUrl",
        "summary": "Point a public URL at another port",
        "tags": [
          "public-urls"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/PublicUrlId"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UpdatePublicUrl"
              },
              "example": {
                "port": 8000
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Updated.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PublicUrl"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Bad port.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer, or public URLs are not enabled."
          }
        }
      },
      "delete": {
        "operationId": "deletePublicUrl",
        "summary": "Remove a public URL (the app keeps running)",
        "tags": [
          "public-urls"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/PublicUrlId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "204": {
            "description": "Removed."
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer, or public URLs are not enabled."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/services": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "listComputerApps",
        "summary": "List the apps that run on a computer, with their state",
        "description": "An app is a command a Linux computer keeps running under its own process manager (supervisord): started at boot, started again when it exits (by its restart policy), and back by itself after a reboot, a crash, a host reboot, a restore or a wake. A running computer is asked for each app’s state (one command on the computer; never a wake). Any other computer, or any computer with live=0, is answered from the last state on file, with live: false. Answers { supported: false, services: [] } for a computer that cannot have apps (only Linux computers on Orgo’s hosts can).",
        "tags": [
          "apps"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "name": "live",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "0"
              ]
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The apps.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ComputerAppList"
                },
                "example": {
                  "supported": true,
                  "computer": "running",
                  "live": true,
                  "limit": 20,
                  "services": [
                    {
                      "id": "2c9a1f0e-7b3d-4e5a-9c8b-1a2b3c4d5e6f",
                      "name": "web",
                      "kind": "command",
                      "deploy_project_id": null,
                      "command": "npm start",
                      "cwd": "/root/app",
                      "env": {
                        "NODE_ENV": "production"
                      },
                      "secret_env_keys": [
                        "DATABASE_URL"
                      ],
                      "port": 3000,
                      "restart": "always",
                      "run_as": "root",
                      "enabled": true,
                      "status": "running",
                      "status_detail": "pid 812, uptime 2:14:09",
                      "status_at": "2026-10-18T09:00:00.000Z",
                      "listening": true,
                      "listening_publicly": true,
                      "applied": true,
                      "error": null,
                      "public_url": "https://cool-thing.orgo.dev",
                      "created_at": "2026-10-18T07:00:00.000Z",
                      "updated_at": "2026-10-18T07:00:00.000Z"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "No access to this computer, view-only access, or a share-link guest."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Computer not found."
          }
        }
      },
      "post": {
        "operationId": "addComputerApp",
        "summary": "Add an app to a computer",
        "description": "Body: { name, command, cwd?, port?, restart?, run_as?, enabled?, env?, secret_env? }. name: 1-32 lowercase letters, digits and hyphens, unique on the computer. command runs with bash in cwd (default the user’s home), after /root/.env and the app’s variables are loaded; values are used as typed. restart: always (default), on-failure (started again after a non-zero exit; an exit in its first 3 seconds counts as a failed start and is retried) or no (once per boot). run_as: root by default. port: what the app listens on, unique on the computer; the computer’s own ports (22, 3389, 5900-5999, 6080-6099, 8080, 9000) are refused. secret_env values are stored encrypted and never returned (only their names, in secret_env_keys). Applied at once when the computer is running (apply.state \"applied\"); otherwise saved and applied when it next runs (\"pending\"). Never wakes the computer. At most 20 apps a computer.",
        "tags": [
          "apps"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CreateComputerApp"
              },
              "example": {
                "name": "web",
                "command": "npm start",
                "cwd": "/root/app",
                "port": 3000,
                "env": {
                  "NODE_ENV": "production"
                },
                "secret_env": {
                  "DATABASE_URL": "postgres://…"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Added.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ComputerAppWrite"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "A field is not valid (INVALID_NAME, INVALID_COMMAND, INVALID_CWD, INVALID_PORT, INVALID_RESTART, INVALID_RUN_AS, INVALID_ENV), the apps are too large to apply together (SERVICES_TOO_LARGE), or the computer cannot have apps (SERVICES_UNSUPPORTED).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "No access to this computer, view-only access, or a share-link guest."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "The name or the port is taken on this computer (NAME_TAKEN, PORT_TAKEN), or it has 20 apps (SERVICE_LIMIT).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/services/{serviceId}": {
      "patch": {
        "operationId": "updateComputerApp",
        "summary": "Change an app",
        "description": "Any of the create fields. env replaces the app’s variables; secret_env changes single secrets: a value sets one, null removes one, and secrets left out are kept. Applied like a create. An app that belongs to a deploy is changed from its deploy (409 MANAGED_BY_DEPLOY).",
        "tags": [
          "apps"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ServiceId"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UpdateComputerApp"
              },
              "example": {
                "command": "npm run serve",
                "secret_env": {
                  "OLD_TOKEN": null
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Changed.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ComputerAppWrite"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "A field is not valid.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Name or port taken, changed meanwhile (CHANGED), or a deploy’s app (MANAGED_BY_DEPLOY)."
          }
        }
      },
      "delete": {
        "operationId": "deleteComputerApp",
        "summary": "Remove an app (it is stopped, and its files and log are removed)",
        "tags": [
          "apps"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ServiceId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "{ deleted: true, apply }: apply.state \"pending\" when the computer is not running; it is removed there when it next runs.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "deleted": {
                      "type": "boolean"
                    },
                    "apply": {
                      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ComputerAppApply"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "A deploy’s app (MANAGED_BY_DEPLOY)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/services/{serviceId}/restart": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "restartComputerApp",
        "summary": "Restart an app on a running computer",
        "tags": [
          "apps"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ServiceId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "{ id, status, status_detail, error }"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "The computer is not running (COMPUTER_NOT_RUNNING; it is never woken for this), or the app is off (SERVICE_OFF)."
          },
          "502": {
            "description": "The computer did not answer, or could not take the change."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/services/{serviceId}/logs": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "getComputerAppLog",
        "summary": "The last lines of an app’s output (stdout and stderr together)",
        "tags": [
          "apps"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ServiceId"
          },
          {
            "name": "lines",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1,
              "maximum": 1000,
              "default": 200
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "{ id, name, lines, found, log }. found is false before the app first wrote anything.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "id": {
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    "name": {
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    "lines": {
                      "type": "integer"
                    },
                    "found": {
                      "type": "boolean"
                    },
                    "log": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "The computer is not running (COMPUTER_NOT_RUNNING)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/deploy-projects": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "listDeployProjects",
        "summary": "List a computer’s GitHub deploys, with their newest deployments",
        "description": "Deploy from GitHub: a repository built on the computer (on every push through the Orgo GitHub App, or by hand for a public repository by URL), run as one of its apps and served at its public URL. Answers { enabled, supported, computer, limit, github, projects }; github lists the workspace’s linked GitHub accounts (installations) for an import. 404 DEPLOYS_DISABLED where deploys are off. Never calls the computer.",
        "tags": [
          "deploys"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The deploys.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DeployProjectList"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "No access to this computer, view-only access, or a share-link guest."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Computer not found, or deploys are off (DEPLOYS_DISABLED)."
          }
        }
      },
      "post": {
        "operationId": "importDeployProject",
        "summary": "Import a GitHub repository and deploy it",
        "description": "Body: { installation_id, repo_id } (a repository a GitHub account linked to the workspace reads) or { repo_url } (a public repository, https://github.com/owner/name; deploys by hand only), plus name?, branch? (default: the repository’s default), root_dir?, framework? (auto, node, python, dockerfile, compose, static), port? (3000), health_path? (/), install_cmd?, build_cmd?, start_cmd?, auto_deploy?, env? and deploy? (false: import only). Detection when framework is auto: orgo.json, a compose file, a Dockerfile, package.json (npm, pnpm, yarn or bun by lockfile; Node.js from .nvmrc or engines, 22 by default), a Python project (uv; a Procfile web: line or a start command), index.html. The app must listen on 0.0.0.0:<port>; it gets PORT. env values are stored encrypted, never returned, and masked in build logs. The first deployment is queued and built once the computer runs; nothing wakes it. At most 5 deploys a computer, and each is one of its 20 apps.",
        "tags": [
          "deploys"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CreateDeployProject"
              },
              "example": {
                "repo_url": "https://github.com/vercel/next-learn",
                "root_dir": "basics/demo",
                "port": 3000,
                "env": {
                  "NEXT_PUBLIC_API": "https://api.example.com"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Imported; its first deployment is in deployments.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DeployProject"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "A field is not valid (INVALID_*), or the repository is not public (REPO_NOT_PUBLIC).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "The installation is not linked to the workspace (INSTALLATION_NOT_FOUND), or the App cannot see the repository (REPO_NOT_FOUND)."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Name or port taken (NAME_TAKEN, PORT_TAKEN), or the computer has the most deploys or apps it can have (PROJECT_LIMIT, SERVICE_LIMIT)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/deploy-projects/{projectId}": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "getDeployProject",
        "summary": "One deploy, with its newest 20 deployments",
        "tags": [
          "deploys"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ProjectId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The deploy.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DeployProject"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          }
        }
      },
      "patch": {
        "operationId": "updateDeployProject",
        "summary": "Change a deploy’s settings",
        "description": "Any of branch, root_dir, framework, port, health_path, install_cmd, build_cmd, start_cmd, auto_deploy. The name cannot change. Changes apply from the next deploy; a port change moves its app and public URL and builds the live commit again. When the computer already has a URL on the new port, the one the deploy made goes and that build takes the one already there.",
        "tags": [
          "deploys"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ProjectId"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UpdateDeployProject"
              },
              "example": {
                "branch": "production",
                "auto_deploy": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Changed.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DeployProject"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "A field is not valid."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Port taken (PORT_TAKEN)."
          }
        }
      },
      "delete": {
        "operationId": "deleteDeployProject",
        "summary": "Remove a deploy: its app, builds, releases, deployments and logs",
        "tags": [
          "deploys"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ProjectId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "{ deleted: true, cleaned }: cleaned is false when the computer was not running (its folder stays until removed by hand). The public URL its deploy made goes too, whether or not the computer runs; one the computer already had on the port stays."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/deploy-projects/{projectId}/env": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "listDeployVariables",
        "summary": "A deploy’s variable names (values are never returned)",
        "tags": [
          "deploys"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ProjectId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "{ env_keys: string[] }"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          }
        }
      },
      "patch": {
        "operationId": "updateDeployVariables",
        "summary": "Set or remove a deploy’s variables",
        "description": "Body: { env: { NAME: \"value\" | null } }: a value sets that variable, null removes it, names left out are kept. Uppercase names. They apply from the next deploy.",
        "tags": [
          "deploys"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ProjectId"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "env": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "additionalProperties": {
                      "type": [
                        "string",
                        "null"
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              "example": {
                "env": {
                  "DATABASE_URL": "postgres://…",
                  "OLD_KEY": null
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "{ env_keys: string[] }"
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "A name or value is not valid (INVALID_ENV)."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/deploy-projects/{projectId}/deployments": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "listDeployments",
        "summary": "A deploy’s newest 20 deployments",
        "tags": [
          "deploys"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ProjectId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "{ deployments }",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "deployments": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Deployment"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          }
        }
      },
      "post": {
        "operationId": "createDeployment",
        "summary": "Deploy now: the branch’s newest commit, or { commit_sha } again",
        "description": "Queued, and built once the computer runs and no other build runs there (one at a time per computer). A newer deploy of the same project supersedes one still queued. A build stops after 30 minutes; a new release that does not answer on its port within 60 seconds is rolled back to the previous one.",
        "tags": [
          "deploys"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ProjectId"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": false,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "commit_sha": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{40}$"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "202": {
            "description": "Queued.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Deployment"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "The GitHub app no longer reaches the repository (PROJECT_DISABLED)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/deployments/{deploymentId}": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "getDeployment",
        "summary": "One deployment",
        "tags": [
          "deploys"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/DeploymentId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The deployment.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Deployment"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/deployments/{deploymentId}/logs": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "getDeploymentLog",
        "summary": "A deployment’s build log, from a cursor",
        "description": "Answers { state, phase, error, log, next, more }: the log after chunk `after`, and the cursor to ask from next. Ask every few seconds while state is queued or running. Variable values are masked.",
        "tags": [
          "deploys"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/DeploymentId"
          },
          {
            "name": "after",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0,
              "default": 0
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The log."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/deployments/{deploymentId}/cancel": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "cancelDeployment",
        "summary": "Cancel a queued or running deployment (the live release stays live)",
        "tags": [
          "deploys"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/DeploymentId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Cancelled (a queued one) or being cancelled (a running one).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Deployment"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Already finished (NOT_ACTIVE)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/deployments/{deploymentId}/rollback": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "rollbackDeployment",
        "summary": "Put an earlier deployment’s release live again, without a build",
        "description": "Only a deployment that went live. The computer keeps the newest 3 releases; an older one fails with release_gone (deploy its commit again instead).",
        "tags": [
          "deploys"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/DeploymentId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "202": {
            "description": "Queued.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Deployment"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Not a deployment that went live (NOT_ROLLBACKABLE), or its release is live now, through it or another deployment (ALREADY_LIVE)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/domains": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "listCustomDomains",
        "summary": "List a computer’s custom domains, each with the DNS records to set",
        "description": "enabled is false while custom domains are off in this environment, or for a computer they cannot serve (reason says so); the list still shows what the computer has. limit is the plan’s cap across every computer of the workspace owner (-1 = unlimited) and used what counts against it. cname_target is where a subdomain’s CNAME points and apex_ipv4 the A record for an apex domain.",
        "tags": [
          "public-urls"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The domains.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "enabled": {
                      "type": "boolean"
                    },
                    "reason": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "Why enabled is false for this computer, when that is the reason."
                    },
                    "limit": {
                      "type": "integer"
                    },
                    "used": {
                      "type": "integer"
                    },
                    "cname_target": {
                      "type": [
                        "string",
                        "null"
                      ],
                      "example": "edge.orgo.dev"
                    },
                    "apex_ipv4": {
                      "type": [
                        "string",
                        "null"
                      ]
                    },
                    "domains": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CustomDomain"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "No access to this computer, or a share-link guest."
          }
        }
      },
      "post": {
        "operationId": "addCustomDomain",
        "summary": "Serve a port on the computer from a domain you own",
        "description": "Body: { \"domain\": \"app.example.com\", \"target_port\"?: 1-65535 } (default 8642; the computer’s own ports are refused). Set every record in dns_records at your DNS provider (a TXT record proving ownership, and a CNAME to the edge, or an A record for an apex domain), then POST /verify. A name under orgo.dev, where public URLs live, is refused (400 INVALID_DOMAIN). A name held by another account that was never verified within 7 days is taken over.",
        "tags": [
          "public-urls"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "domain"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "domain": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "target_port": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 1,
                    "maximum": 65535
                  }
                }
              },
              "example": {
                "domain": "app.example.com",
                "target_port": 3000
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Added, waiting for DNS.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CustomDomain"
                },
                "example": {
                  "id": "0b8e6a1c-5d4f-4e3a-8b2c-1d0e9f8a7b6c",
                  "domain": "app.example.com",
                  "status": "pending",
                  "target_port": 3000,
                  "dns": {
                    "type": "TXT",
                    "name": "_orgo-verify.app.example.com",
                    "value": "9f2c4e6a8b0d1f3e5a7c9e1b3d5f7a9c"
                  },
                  "dns_records": [
                    {
                      "type": "TXT",
                      "name": "_orgo-verify.app.example.com",
                      "value": "9f2c4e6a8b0d1f3e5a7c9e1b3d5f7a9c"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "CNAME",
                      "name": "app.example.com",
                      "value": "edge.orgo.dev"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Invalid domain or port (INVALID_DOMAIN, INVALID_PORT), or a computer custom domains cannot serve (CUSTOM_DOMAINS_UNSUPPORTED).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "Plan limit, no access, or a share-link guest."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Custom domains are not enabled (CUSTOM_DOMAINS_NOT_ENABLED).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "That domain is already in use."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/domains/{domainId}": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "getCustomDomain",
        "summary": "Get one custom domain with its DNS records",
        "tags": [
          "public-urls"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "name": "domainId",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "format": "uuid"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The domain.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CustomDomain"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          }
        }
      },
      "patch": {
        "operationId": "updateCustomDomain",
        "summary": "Point a custom domain at another port",
        "description": "Live within seconds. The computer’s own ports are refused, as for a public URL.",
        "tags": [
          "public-urls"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "name": "domainId",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "format": "uuid"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UpdateCustomDomain"
              },
              "example": {
                "target_port": 8000
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Updated.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CustomDomain"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Bad port (INVALID_PORT), or a computer custom domains cannot serve (CUSTOM_DOMAINS_UNSUPPORTED).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthenticated."
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "No access, a share-link guest, or a view-only member."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer, or custom domains are not enabled (CUSTOM_DOMAINS_NOT_ENABLED)."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Orgo turned the domain off ({ status: \"disabled\" })."
          }
        }
      },
      "delete": {
        "operationId": "deleteCustomDomain",
        "summary": "Remove a custom domain",
        "tags": [
          "public-urls"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "name": "domainId",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "format": "uuid"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "{ deleted: true }"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Orgo turned the domain off ({ status: \"disabled\" }); contact support to remove it."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/computers/{id}/domains/{domainId}/verify": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "verifyCustomDomain",
        "summary": "Check the TXT record and where the domain points, and turn it on",
        "tags": [
          "public-urls"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ComputerId"
          },
          {
            "name": "domainId",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "format": "uuid"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "{ status: \"active\" }"
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "A computer custom domains cannot serve (CUSTOM_DOMAINS_UNSUPPORTED).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "Custom-domain limit reached."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found on this computer, or custom domains are not enabled (CUSTOM_DOMAINS_NOT_ENABLED)."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "The TXT record is not visible yet ({ status: \"verifying\" }); the TXT record is there but the domain does not point at the edge yet ({ status: \"verifying\", code: \"DNS_NOT_POINTED\", dns_records }); or Orgo turned the domain off ({ status: \"disabled\" }).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "status": "verifying",
                  "code": "DNS_NOT_POINTED",
                  "error": "Point app.example.com at edge.orgo.dev (CNAME record), then verify again.",
                  "dns_records": [
                    {
                      "type": "TXT",
                      "name": "_orgo-verify.app.example.com",
                      "value": "9f2c4e6a8b0d1f3e5a7c9e1b3d5f7a9c"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "CNAME",
                      "name": "app.example.com",
                      "value": "edge.orgo.dev"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
